        "gen_ai.tool.call.result": "README.md (940 bytes)\n     1→# greet-pkg\n     2→\n     3→A minimal Node.js package that exports a simple greeting function.\n     4→\n     5→## Install\n     6→\n     7→```bash\n     8→npm install greet-pkg\n     9→```\n    10→\n    11→## Usage\n    12→\n    13→```js\n    14→const { greet } = require(\"./index\");\n    15→\n    16→greet();        // \"Hello, world!\"\n    17→greet(\"Ada\");   // \"Hello, Ada!\"\n    18→```\n    19→\n    20→## API\n    21→\n    22→### `greet(name?)`\n    23→\n    24→Returns the string `Hello, <name>!`. Defaults to `\"world\"` when `name` is omitted.\n    25→\n    26→## Integrity and reproducibility\n    27→\n    28→- Exact SHA-256 hashes of the source and manifest files (`index.js`, `package.json`, `README.md`) are recorded in `checksums.txt` (standard `sha256sum` format).\n    29→- Verify the inputs have not changed:\n    30→\n    31→  ```bash\n    32→  sha256sum -c checksums.txt\n    33→  ```\n    34→\n    35→- Regenerate `checksums.txt` after an intentional change:\n    36→\n    37→  ```bash\n    38→  npm run hash\n    39→  ```\n    40→\n    41→- Dependencies: none. Any dependency added in the future must be declared in `package.json` with an exact pinned version (no `^` or `~` ranges) so dependency inputs stay reproducible.\n    42→\n    43→## License\n    44→\n    45→MIT\n    46→",
